  "result": "I fixed it, and the command now prints **27.06**.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded the decimal part on the wrong side. It used `rjust`, so `\"12.5\"` turned the fraction `\"5\"` into `\"05\"` and became 1205 cents instead of 1250. The fix was changing `rjust` to `ljust`, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`.\n\n**Tests:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest discover`, and all 6 tests pass.",
